{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01M5AUThJv9Ly3CobFzQRHWm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a personal productivity + R&D mission-control system built for J.C. Liechty. Grounded claims from the project docs:\n\n**Purpose**\n- It's a single-user productivity system that manages tasks, projects, and ideas across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing), all living in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`) with **plain markdown files as the source of truth** â€” no database, no syncing.\n\n**What it does**\n- Runs as a **persistent local web server** (`anchor_gui.py`) on `http://localhost:8777`, owned by the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. The browser dashboard reads/writes the markdown files directly and logs every change.\n- Provides a full **task lifecycle** (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored) editable both from the GUI and a mirrored CLI (`anchor.py`), plus a quick-capture inbox and per-domain views.\n- Has grown a substantial **R&D \"control surface\"** (v2â†’v4) that turns each project into a cockpit for \"trio\"-driven work â€” the Research (researchPrime) â†’ Planning (Crucible) â†’ Build (Foreman) skill pipeline. This includes per-lane session tracking, cached/validated AI-generated summaries, real **ConPTY interactive terminals** with per-session git-worktree isolation, an engine toggle (Claude/Gemini), cost/token/time rollups, grass-catcher idea promotion, and type-aware deliverable launching.\n- Self-tests via `anchor_healthcheck.py` daily at 5 AM, walking the v2/v3/v4 surfaces fully stubbed (no live `claude`, never touching port 8777 or real data).\n\n**What it ships**\n- The declared deliverable is **`anchor_gui.py`** â€” the self-contained stdlib-only Python HTTP server + dashboard.\n- Supporting modules: the CLI engine (`anchor.py`), R&D surface modules (`rnd_registry.py`, `sessions.py`, `summarizer.py`, `effort_history.py`, `pty_manager.py`, `terminal_session.py`, `deliverables.py`, etc.), vendored frontend assets (xterm.js, anchor-term, GWL brand mark), and the markdown data files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`).\n- **Stdlib-only** with exactly one declared native exception: optional `pywinpty` for the terminal subsystem (`pip install .[terminal]`), which degrades gracefully if absent.\n\nOne caveat on grounding: the \"North Star\" / \"locked decisions\" anchors you quoted describe the v4 cockpit *design intent*; per CLAUDE.md these were **built (9 waves GREEN, 637 passed) and merged to master** (commit `38fd70e`) as of 2026-06-13 â€” so they're shipped, not just planned."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8ac6e07-7592-483c-8174-5e8f64344119","uuid":"29580fdf-e642-4d1c-af30-9a3bfd8d9591","request_id":"req_011Cc1fQhP9b5sGwADD1zXas"}
